  "notes": "{召|め}し{上|あ}がる is the honorific form for both {食|た}べる (to eat) and {飲|の}む (to drink).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]を召し上がる\n\nKEIGO TYPE:\n{尊敬語|そんけいご} (honorific) - used when speaking about someone of higher status.\n\nCOMMON PHRASES:\n- どうぞ{召|め}し{上|あ}がってください: Please help yourself\n- {何|なに}を{召|め}し{上|あ}がりますか: What would you like?\n\nKEIGO RELATIONSHIPS:\n- Plain: {食|た}べる / {飲|の}む\n- Honorific: {召|め}し{上|あ}がる (about others)\n- Humble: いただく (about oneself)",
